<title>UZBEKISTAN: Uzbek Jan-Sept crude oil output up 1.2 percent.</title>
<headline>Uzbek Jan-Sept crude oil output up 1.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>TASHKENT 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uzbekistan's production of crude oil and gas condensate for the first nine months of 1996 increased 1.2 percent over the same period last year, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The committee released the following figures for energy output in its latest statistical review:</p>
<p> UZBEK ENERGY OUTPUT		    Sept 1996     Jan-Sept 1996</p>
<p> Crude oil (million tonnes)		 0.7	  5.6</p>
<p>  yr/yr pct change			   -5.1	  1.2</p>
<p> Natural gas (billion cubic metres)     3.6	 35.9</p>
<p>  yr/yr pct change			    2.6	  0.5</p>
<p> Gasoline (tonnes)			  111,500    948,700</p>
<p>  yr/yr pct change			   -1.6	 -0.4</p>
<p> Diesel (tonnes)			    190,600  1,426,200</p>
<p>  yr/yr pct change			  -33.8	-13.0</p>
<p> Fuel oil (mazut) (tonnes)		204,700  1,776,000</p>
<p>  yr/yr change				 -4.3	+10.5</p>
<p>-- Almaty Newsroom +7 3272 509 410</p>
